  "objective_summary": "Landed ParallelFrontier@1 deterministic readiness and conflict-free frontier selection. Every readiness condition (active plan, legal lifecycle, predecessors, semantic binding, capsule/source fallback, contracts/obligations, scope, active-writer conflicts, resources/provider capacity, completion policy, quarantine/supersession/block/review) is enforced fail-closed before a task enters the ready set. The ready set is projected through the dedicated semantic conflict graph; a resource-feasible conflict-free antichain is selected with policy-versioned scaled-integer scoring (completion, critical-path, unlock, locality, age/fairness minus resource/model cost, provider pressure, merge risk, uncertainty, retry cost). Small frontiers use exact search; larger ones use deterministic greedy-plus-local-improvement. Stable task identity is the final tie-break. Every rejection and selection is receipted. Model proposals are accepted as non-authoritative input and never admit work or alter the selected antichain. Binary floats are excluded from content-addressed identities. Worker completion or task status alone never authorizes acceptance.",
